    <bpmn:process id="W_W1501" name="W1501. Store Rooftop Solar Panel Installation ROI Assessment, Net Metering Application &amp; Monthly Energy Offset Tracking" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual sustainability infrastructure review; also triggered when new store construction is planned or when a store&#x27;s electricity cost exceeds PHP 200,000/month
Frequency: Annual assessment cycle; per-store installation project (one-time); monthly energy offset tracking post-installation
Volume: ~80 commissioned solar sites today (per W3457), growing at ~10–30 sites/year toward the ~205-rooftop potential (per VS-108); ~10–15 retrofit assessments/year for the next tranche
Owner: Facilities Manager
Participants: Facilities Manager, Sustainability Officer, CFO, Solar EPC Contractor, MERALCO/Local Electric Cooperative, Energy Regulatory Commission (ERC)
Source: workflow W1501 — Store Rooftop Solar Panel Installation ROI Assessment, Net Metering Application &amp; Monthly Energy Offset Tracking</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1501_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1501_Lane1" name="Facilities Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1501_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1501_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1501_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1501_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1501_Lane2" name="Solar EPC Contractor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1501_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1501_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1501_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1501_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1501_Start5" name="Annual sustainability infrastructure review; also triggered when new store construction…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1501_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1501_Task6" name="Annual solar candidate assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Annual solar candidate assessment: Annual: (a) Facilities Manager screens all stores for solar viability: (i) rooftop area: minimum 500 sqm unobstructed flat roof; (ii) structural load capacity: roof must support ~15 kg/sqm additional load from panels and mounting; (iii) shading assessment: nearby buildings or trees that would reduce output by &gt; 20%; (iv) utility provider: MERALCO (Luzon) and major cooperatives (Visayas/Mindanao) must offer net metering; (v) electricity consumption: stores with &gt; PHP 150,000/month electricity cost prioritized; (b) shortlisted stores (~15–20/year) undergo detailed feasibility study
Responsible (R): Facilities Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2–3 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1501_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1501_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1501_Task7" name="ROI analysis &amp; investment approval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: ROI analysis &amp; investment approval: For shortlisted stores: (a) Facilities Manager engages solar EPC contractor for site-specific proposal: (i) system size recommendation (kWp); (ii) estimated annual generation (kWh) based on local solar irradiance data; (iii) installation cost; (iv) projected energy offset (% of consumption); (v) payback period; (vi) 25-year lifetime savings estimate; (b) Sustainability Officer calculates: (i) carbon offset (tons CO2 avoided); (ii) contribution to BuildRight&#x27;s corporate emissions reduction target; (c) CFO evaluates: (i) ROI vs. alternative capital uses; (ii) available incentives (tax exemptions under RA 9513, DOE renewable energy certificates); (iii) financing options (outright purchase, lease, or PPA — Power Purchase Agreement); (d) approved installations added to capital expenditure plan
Responsible (R): Facilities Manager / Sustainability Officer
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–3 weeks per batch</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1501_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1501_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1501_Task8" name="Net metering application &amp; utility interconnection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Net metering application &amp; utility interconnection: (a) Facilities Manager submits net metering application to the local utility (MERALCO or electric cooperative): (i) ERC net metering application form; (ii) electrical single-line diagram of the proposed system; (iii) building permit; (iv) electrical permit; (v) solar system specifications; (b) utility reviews application (typically 30–60 days); (c) utility conducts site inspection; (d) interconnection agreement signed; (e) bidirectional meter installed replacing standard meter; (f) system commissioning and parallel operation test with utility witness
Responsible (R): Facilities Manager / Solar EPC Contractor
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 60–90 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1501_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1501_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1501_Task9" name="Installation project execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Installation project execution: (a) Solar EPC contractor manages installation: (i) structural reinforcement if needed; (ii) mounting system installation; (iii) panel placement and wiring; (iv) inverter installation and grid connection; (v) monitoring system setup; (b) Facilities Manager monitors project progress against timeline; (c) safety compliance: working-at-height permits, electrical safety protocols per PA-24.1; (d) system commissioned and tested; (e) handover to BuildRight facilities team with as-built documentation and O&amp;M manual
Responsible (R): Solar EPC Contractor / Facilities Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 4–8 weeks per store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1501_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1501_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1501_Task10" name="Monthly energy offset tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monthly energy offset tracking: Post-installation: (a) solar monitoring system reports daily/monthly: (i) energy generated (kWh); (ii) energy consumed from grid (kWh); (iii) energy exported to grid (kWh); (iv) net energy (import − export); (v) estimated savings vs. pre-solar baseline; (b) Facilities Manager reviews monthly report for each solar store; (c) underperforming systems (&lt; 80% of projected output) flagged for investigation: (i) panel soiling (dust, bird droppings); (ii) inverter malfunction; (iii) shading from new construction; (d) quarterly: panel cleaning scheduled for stores in dusty areas (near construction sites); (e) annual: system health check by solar contractor including thermal imaging of panels
Responsible (R): System / Facilities Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2–3 hours/month for all solar stores</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1501_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1501_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1501_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1501_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1501_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-303 (ensure controlled execution — Facility Maintenance &amp; Equipment (PA-20.3).) | - operational: Facilities Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Facilities Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1501_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1501_Annotation12" targetRef="W1501_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1501_Flow14" sourceRef="W1501_Start5" targetRef="W1501_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1501_Flow15" sourceRef="W1501_Task6" targetRef="W1501_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1501_Flow16" sourceRef="W1501_Task7" targetRef="W1501_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1501_Flow17" sourceRef="W1501_Task8" targetRef="W1501_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1501_Flow18" sourceRef="W1501_Task9" targetRef="W1501_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1501_Flow19" sourceRef="W1501_Task10" targetRef="W1501_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1501_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1501_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1501">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1501_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1501_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1501_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1501_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1501_Lane3_di" bpmnElement="W1501_Lane3" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="420" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1501_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W1501_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1501_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1501_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
