    <bpmn:process id="W_W1564" name="W1564. Store Waste Management, Construction Material Scrap Disposal, Cardboard Baling &amp; Recycling Revenue Recovery" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Daily store operations; weekly waste disposal cycle; monthly recycling revenue reconciliation; or annual waste management contract renewal
Frequency: Daily waste collection per store; weekly cardboard baling; monthly recycling revenue reconciliation; annual contract review
Volume: Per store: ~2–4 cubic meters of waste per day (cardboard packaging ~50%, plastic wrap ~15%, damaged merchandise ~10%, general waste ~25%); chain-wide: ~400–800 cubic meters/day; ~PHP 5–10M annual waste disposal cost offset by ~PHP 2–4M recycling revenue
Owner: Facilities Manager
Participants: Facilities Manager, Maintenance/Utility (store), Waste Management Contractor, Category Manager (damaged goods disposition), Finance (recycling revenue), Sustainability Officer
Source: workflow W1564 — Store Waste Management, Construction Material Scrap Disposal, Cardboard Baling &amp; Recycling Revenue Recovery</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1564_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1564_Lane1" name="Maintenance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1564_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1564_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1564_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1564_Lane2" name="Facilities Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1564_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1564_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1564_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1564_Lane3" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1564_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1564_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1564_Start5" name="Daily store operations; weekly waste disposal cycle; monthly recycling revenue…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1564_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1564_Task6" name="In-store waste source separation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: In-store waste source separation: Maintenance/Utility maintains waste separation at each store: (a) Cardboard/Paper: designated bin in receiving area — all cardboard boxes flattened and placed in bin; (b) Plastic: separate bin for shrink wrap, plastic straps, plastic bags; (c) Wood: pallets stacked in designated area (reusable pallets separated from broken pallets); (d) Damaged Merchandise: segregated by disposition — (i) returnable to vendor per W1391, (ii) recyclable (metal, certain plastics), (iii) hazardous waste per W142 (paint, solvents, chemicals — separate hazmat bin), (iv) general waste (broken tiles, contaminated materials); (e) General Waste: non-recyclable waste in standard bins for landfill disposal
Responsible (R): Maintenance/Utility
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Ongoing (part of daily duties)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1564_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1564_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1564_Task7" name="Cardboard baling operation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Cardboard baling operation: Weekly: (a) Maintenance/Utility operates the store&#x27;s cardboard baler (1 per store): (i) load flattened cardboard into baler, (ii) compress into bale (~100–150 kg per bale), (iii) tie bale with wire, (iv) stage bale for recycling buyer pickup; (b) each store produces ~8–15 bales/month (~800–2,250 kg of cardboard); (c) chain-wide: ~1,600–3,000 bales/month (~160,000–450,000 kg); (d) safety: Maintenance/Utility trained on baler operation per W140 equipment safety; baler guard must be in place before operation
Responsible (R): Maintenance/Utility
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/week/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1564_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1564_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1564_Task8" name="Recycling buyer management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Recycling buyer management: Facilities Manager coordinates recycling buyers: (a) contract with 2–3 recycling companies per region for cardboard, plastic, and metal pickup; (b) buyers collect baled cardboard from stores on scheduled routes (weekly or bi-weekly); (c) payment: per-kg rate based on prevailing market price (cardboard: PHP 3–5/kg; plastic: PHP 2–4/kg; metal: PHP 10–15/kg); (d) each store&#x27;s recycling revenue credited monthly: estimated PHP 2,500–5,000/store/month from cardboard alone; (e) Finance reconciles recycling revenue monthly against waste disposal cost
Responsible (R): Facilities Manager / Finance
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1564_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1564_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1564_Task9" name="Damaged merchandise disposition">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Damaged merchandise disposition: For damaged merchandise identified during receiving per W3 or cycle counting per W42: (a) Category Manager authorizes disposition: (i) return to vendor for credit per W1391 (vendor-caused damage), (ii) markdown and sell at discount per W86 clearance (customer-damaged packaging but product intact), (iii) donate per W1106 (functional but cosmetically damaged), (iv) recycle (metal tools, certain plastics), (v) dispose (contaminated, hazardous, or non-recyclable); (b) Maintenance/Utility executes disposition per Category Manager authorization
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Maintenance/Utility
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1564_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1564_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1564_Task10" name="Hazardous waste disposal">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Hazardous waste disposal: For hazardous waste (paint, solvents, adhesives, chemicals) per W142 hazmat management: (a) store in designated hazmat storage area with proper containment; (b) quarterly pickup by DENR-licensed hazardous waste transporter per DOC-007; (c) manifest documentation maintained per environmental regulations; (d) cost: ~PHP 50,000–100,000/store/year for hazmat disposal; (e) Sustainability Officer tracks hazardous waste volume and disposal compliance
Responsible (R): Facilities Manager / Sustainability Officer
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1564_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1564_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1564_Task11" name="Annual waste management review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Annual waste management review: Facilities Manager reviews waste program annually: (a) total waste generated by store and category; (b) recycling rate (recycled waste ÷ total waste × 100; target: &gt; 60%); (c) recycling revenue vs. disposal cost; (d) vendor return rate (damaged merchandise returned to vendor ÷ total damaged merchandise); (e) identify stores with low recycling rates for operational improvement; (f) renegotiate recycling buyer contracts based on volume
Responsible (R): Facilities Manager / Finance
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 4 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1564_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1564_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1564_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1564_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1564_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-303 (ensure controlled execution — Facility Maintenance &amp; Equipment (PA-20.3).) | - operational: Facilities Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Facilities Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1564_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1564_Annotation13" targetRef="W1564_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
