    <bpmn:process id="W_W5565" name="W5565. Third-Party Construction Damage &amp; Adjacent-Works Response Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: A neighbor&#x27;s or adjacent party&#x27;s construction works damage BuildRight-occupied or banked property — excavation undermining foundations or triggering settlement cracks, vibration damage to glazing/racking/stock, scaffolding or crane over-swing over the building, or a cut utility line (water/power/telecom) during adjacent works
Frequency: Episodic urban-density event class: a handful of substantiated damage events per year across ~205 sites (stores fronting busy commercial streets, DCs beside industrial development, banked parcels beside new builds); multi-week adjacent works also drive precautionary monitoring even without substantiated damage
Volume: 1 event × 1 site × the damage-surface scope (structure, glazing, racking, stock, utilities) × the dispute track (evidence, claim, possible legal action)
Owner: Facilities Manager (event owner); Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate (portfolio &amp; claim posture)
Participants: Store/DC Manager (site), Structural Engineer, VS-26 insurance (W876), Legal (VS-100 demand &amp; dispute), the adjacent contractor/owner and its CAR insurer, LGU building official (permits leverage), VS-178 land team where banked parcels are affected (W5133 survey interface), BCP (W848-class reporting for prolonged events)
Source: workflow W5565 — Third-Party Construction Damage &amp; Adjacent-Works Response Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5565_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5565_Lane1" name="Site Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5565_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5565_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5565_Lane2" name="Facilities">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5565_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5565_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5565_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5565_Lane3" name="Structural Engineer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5565_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5565_Lane4" name="Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5565_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5565_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5565_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5565_Start6" name="A neighbor&#x27;s or adjacent party&#x27;s construction works damage BuildRight-occupied or banked…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5565_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5565_Task7" name="Make-safe &amp; notify">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Make-safe &amp; notify: stop-work request to the adjacent contractor where damage is active; isolate affected utilities; cordon damage zones (W330 mechanics if during trading)
Responsible (R): Site Manager / Facilities
Accountable (A): Facilities Manager
Duration: Same day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5565_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5565_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5565_Task8" name="Evidence before repair">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Evidence before repair: dated photo/video crack survey with measuring points; engineering baseline where settlement is suspected; CCTV preservation hold (W838); utility-cut documentation with the utility&#x27;s own records
Responsible (R): Facilities / Structural Engineer
Accountable (A): Facilities Manager
Duration: 24–72 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5565_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5565_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5565_Task9" name="Safety gate">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Safety gate: engineer assessment of affected zones before any reopen — the red-tag discipline; precautionary monitoring regime (crack gauges) while adjacent works continue
Responsible (R): Structural Engineer
Accountable (A): Facilities Manager
Duration: Per assessment</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5565_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5565_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5565_Task10" name="Liability track">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Liability track: notice letter to the adjacent contractor/owner and its CAR insurer early; demand pack assembled from the Step 2 evidence
Responsible (R): Legal / Insurance
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: 1–2 weeks elapsed</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5565_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5565_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5565_Task11" name="Regulatory leverage">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Regulatory leverage: LGU building-official complaint where permits or site-safety rules are violated; stop-work order request for active-risk works
Responsible (R): Legal / Facilities
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Per posture</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5565_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5565_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5565_Task12" name="Claim &amp; recovery">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Claim &amp; recovery: repair execution (own funds where faster, documented for recovery); claim pack via VS-26 (W876) and the third-party CAR claim; disputed claims ride counsel (VS-100) with W5133-grade technical documentation
Responsible (R): Facilities / VS-26
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Per repair scope</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5565_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5565_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5565_Task13" name="Prolonged-works management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Prolonged-works management: monitoring reports and escalation cadence with the neighbor and LGU; BCP reporting where trading is affected (the W848 class); banked-parcel cases coordinate the VS-178 land team
Responsible (R): Facilities / BCP
Accountable (A): Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate
Duration: Per works duration</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5565_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5565_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5565_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5565_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5565_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-303 (ensure controlled execution — Facility Maintenance &amp; Equipment (PA-20.3).) | - operational: evidence captured before any repair is authorized; red-tag/reopen decisions documented with engineer clearance; third-party claim files reconciled to recovery outcomes
Owner: Facilities Manager (event owner); Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate (portfolio &amp; claim posture)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5565_Assoc16" sourceRef="W5565_Annotation15" targetRef="W5565_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
